  "_doc": "The machine-readable Phase-3 row-set — the SINGLE source that drives scripts/golden-bootstrap.cjs and against which the CLAUDE.md Phase-3 tables + the rendered tree are validated three ways. Every row mirrors a parsed CLAUDE.md table cell EXACTLY (node scripts/golden-bootstrap.cjs --dump-tables). The three red-gate scripts, the red-gate hook row, and the LICENSE row all resolve like any other row: the three scripts ship in templates/scripts/, and the red-gate hook + LICENSE rows are in the CLAUDE.md always-generated table, so the --diff is ENFORCING (known-gaps.json emptied). render: 'wiring' = fill {{placeholders}} + scan (deterministic files the bootstrap MUST fill — incl. LICENSE, filled from the owner's holder/year/type); 'copy' = ship the template verbatim (forms keep their placeholders, not scanned); 'empty' = generated empty. tiers/locus/deliverable/app_map encode the conditional rows so Lite/Full/non-hybrid renders do not false-diff. ENUMERATION MODEL: this row-set is ALSO the golden catalog validate-validator-enumeration.cjs reconciles the shipped hooks/scripts/commands against (each is a 1:1 render row here). It is NOT a full-validator catalog: the BAKE copies ALL of validators/ wholesale, while this GOLDEN row-set RENDERS only the HEADLINE validator rows (validate-stage-prompts/retrospective/app-map/test-honesty + README) — the rest are inherited by the bake and enumerated against the DOC catalogs (validators/README.md + the CLAUDE.md/PROJECT-CLAUDE.md scaffold tables, where the enumeration blockquote carries the full set). So per-class catalog scope: validators -> README + the two scaffold-table docs; hooks/scripts/commands -> CLAUDE.md scaffold tables + this row-set. Adding a full validator render row here would change the rendered scaffold COUNT and is deliberately NOT done.",
